title: Global shell › Demo menu › Fast-forward the demo clock
route: Every page (Demo menu › Time)
intro: Fast-forward moves the demo clock by an hour or a day. It only changes what is worked out from the clock: ages, countdowns and 'overdue' wording. It never makes anything happen by itself.
dir: TD
also: The clock starts at Tue 20 Oct 2026, 10:42 am. It has no 'back' button: only 'Reset demo data' returns it.
---
start s1 "Open the Demo menu"
click c1 "Click 'Fast-forward 1 hour'"
click c2 "Click 'Fast-forward 1 day'"
process p1 "Clock moves forward 60 minutes"
process p2 "Clock moves forward 1,440 minutes"
store st1 "Demo clock saved\n(minutes since the start)"
process p3 "'Demo' pill shows the new time\n'Tue 11:42 am' after an hour, 'Wed 10:42 am' after a day"
toast t1 "'Clock moved forward 1 hour' or 'Clock moved forward 1 day'\n'Times in stage and deadlines updated.'"
process p4 "Toast fades after about 4 seconds. Every click adds its own toast. The menu stays open"

group gMove "What moves with the clock"
  process m1 "Case Manager\nTracker 'Clock' column, 'Being prepared' due pills ('Notice due in 5 h' becomes 'Overdue'), the 'Today' day card on Reviews this week"
  process m2 "Notifications\nAges: '16 min ago' becomes '1 h ago'"
  process m3 "Dashboard\nTime in stage, 'late' flags and the 'Outcomes for' date range"
  process m4 "Authorizations, Denial Intelligence\nQueue bands, case clocks, peer-to-peer and appeal deadlines"
  process m5 "Eligibility & Benefits, EMR Connect, New case\nHow long ago a check, a sync or a referral was"
endgroup

group gStill "What does not change"
  process s2 "No payer replies, no referral arrives, no agent finishes a step"
  process s3 "No case changes status, no new notification, no badge changes"
  process s4 "Ask FLO answers and Case Manager review statuses stay as they were"
endgroup

group gHow "How things really arrive in the demo"
  goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Demo controls (payer replies)"
  goto g2 "Continues in: New case › Referral step (sample referrals)"
endgroup

end e1 "Page keeps its place. Click again to move further"

s1 --> c1 & c2
c1 --> p1 --> st1
c2 --> p2 --> st1
st1 --> p3 --> t1 --> p4 --> e1
st1 --> m1 & m2 & m3 & m4 & m5
st1 -.-> s2
s2 --> s3 --> s4
s2 --> g1
s2 --> g2
